  "hypothesis": "After the qualified manual JPEG advancement redesign, immediate parsing still enters public ProbeCore compiler async setup. Complete immediately with the existing typed result; move actual suspension and failure into functional helpers. Profile locations are a lead rather than removable-time attribution. The public wrapper and production parser/owner have materially changed since PCE31; its 2.6percent short point was unconfirmed and the old fixed4.1percent threshold is superseded. No gain is presumed.",
  "intendedEndState": "One nonasync setup/owner-transfer wrapper, one out-of-line pending helper with using(reader), one async failure helper. Keep the shared grammar and acquisition owner unchanged. No new cache,array,pool,field,admission model or public API.",
  "boundaries": "Validation and reader construction remain in the same order. A completed successful typed task is consumed once, then reader disposed before returning the independently owned result. Non-successful tasks transfer the owner to an out-of-line helper, which awaits actual users before disposal. Synchronous setup/parser exceptions enter an async failure helper with using(reader), retaining cancellation status/token even for unsignaled tokens and cleanup exception precedence. A Dispose exception sees the already-disposed idempotent reader. Input/root are borrowed. No parser,read,check,poll,metadata or encoder change.",
